babel-rust: Rust port of the python-babel hot path (number/currency/date
formatting kernels + pattern parsing) with Python bindings.

Upstream project:

  python-babel/babel — https://github.com/python-babel/babel
  Copyright (c) 2013-2026 by the Babel Team, see AUTHORS for more information.
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License (see LICENSE, the upstream text).

The pure-Python fallback in this repository (`babel/numbers.py`,
`babel/dates.py` fallback paths) executes the upstream 2.18.0 logic
verbatim, and the non-hot-path modules are byte-identical copies of the
upstream 2.18.0 sources.

Locale data (`babel/locale-data/*.dat`, `babel/global.dat`) is data
derived from the Unicode Common Locale Data Repository (CLDR) and is
used under the Unicode License Agreement — Data Files and Software;
see LICENSE.unicode. No second copy of CLDR is vendored into the Rust
crate: at runtime the extension receives small per-locale ingredient
bundles (pattern strings, symbols, names) extracted from the installed
data files above, which remain the single source of truth.
